# 14 Extra compile options: PCRE2_EXTRA_MATCH_WORD,
#    PCRE2_EXTRA_MATCH_LINE, PCRE2_EXTRA_BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL and more
# https://www.pcre.org/current/doc/html/pcre2api.html
#
# Not exposed by PHP. The PCRE2_EXTRA_* option word has no PHP surface at
# all except for CASELESS_RESTRICT (the 8.4 'r' modifier). Everything else
# in the family is unreachable.
#
# What it is / what it enables:
#   MATCH_WORD makes the pattern match whole words only, as if wrapped in
#   \b(?:...)\b. That is grep -w as an engine option with no pattern
#   rewriting.
#   MATCH_LINE makes the pattern match complete lines only. That is
#   grep -x.
#   BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL turns an unknown escape like \q into the literal
#   character instead of a compile error. A lenient mode for patterns that
#   come from configuration or user input.
#   ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK re-enables \K inside lookarounds, which PHP 8.5
#   hard-disabled with no way to opt back in.
# (Also unexposed and not demoed here: ESCAPED_CR_IS_LF,
# ALLOW_SURROGATE_ESCAPES, NO_BS0, PYTHON_OCTAL, NEVER_CALLOUT.)

# Expect: 0: cat
# MATCH_WORD: "cat" as a whole word matches...
/cat/match_word
    the cat sat

# Expect: No match
# ...but the "cat" inside "concatenate" does not.
/cat/match_word
    concatenate

# Expect: 0: cat
# MATCH_LINE: the pattern must span a whole line.
/cat/match_line
    cat

# Expect: No match
# A line with anything else on it fails.
/cat/match_line
    a cat

# Expect: 0: q
# BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL: \q is a compile error in PHP. Here it just means
# the literal letter.
/\q/bad_escape_is_literal
    q

# Expect: Start of matched string is beyond its end - displaying from end to start.
#         0: b
# ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK: \K inside a lookaround works again. PHP 8.5's
# compile error even names the option that nothing in PHP can set: "\K
# is not allowed in lookarounds (but see PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK)".
# (The odd first line is pcre2test noting the \K-shifted match start.)
/a(?=b\K)/allow_lookaround_bsk
    ab
